[00:22.46]1. Here with us are aged ones,
[00:29.66]Those whose youth has passed.
[00:36.86]Here among us they endure;
[00:43.86]Still they’re holding fast.
[00:50.86]Loss of strength besets them all;
[00:57.86]Loss of mates for some.
[01:05.95]Father, please confirm their faith
[01:10.76]In the life to come.
[01:15.57](Chorus)
[01:20.39]Father, you remember
[01:27.76]How in faith they’ve run.
[01:35.13]Give them your assurance;
[01:42.37]May they hear, “Well done!”
[02:16.91]2. Splendid is gray-headedness
[02:51.45]Found in ways of right.
[02:58.75]Beautiful are faithful ones
[03:05.75]In Jehovah’s sight.
[03:13.24]May we always recognize
[03:20.44]They were once young too.
[03:30.81]Loyally they gave their best
[03:34.81]When their strength was new.
[03:38.31](Chorus)
[03:41.81]Father, you remember
[03:49.92]How in faith they’ve run.
[03:57.02]Give them your assurance;
[04:04.22]May they hear, “Well done!”